WEBVTT

00:06.930 --> 00:08.890
All of these <i>are</i> right!

00:08.890 --> 00:10.900
The mushroom and zombie were on point.

00:10.900 --> 00:11.930
And this white circle...

00:11.930 --> 00:14.040
It's not a meat bun, it's a golf ball.

00:14.040 --> 00:16.190
This funny-looking one's a jizo statue,

00:16.190 --> 00:18.140
which means the stops coming up...

00:18.140 --> 00:19.680
Kusamochi and a bowl of curry?

00:19.680 --> 00:21.210
They might be completely different.

00:21.210 --> 00:23.210
His other pictures weren't 
very good, either.

00:23.210 --> 00:24.530
But I'm sure he's right!

00:24.530 --> 00:26.640
Then the world disappearing...

00:26.640 --> 00:28.130
That part's wrong!

00:28.130 --> 00:30.770
I knew it'd happen, but not this quickly.

00:30.770 --> 00:32.190
Don't scare us like that!

00:32.190 --> 00:33.500
I didn't come up with it.

00:33.500 --> 00:36.370
It sounds even more true when 
it's coming from you. No thanks.

00:36.370 --> 00:37.650
What if, though?

00:37.650 --> 00:41.100
If the world was going to end, 
when would it happen?

00:41.100 --> 00:43.530
Do you think it'll be after 
we turn into animals?

00:43.530 --> 00:44.940
It better not be sooner!

00:44.940 --> 00:46.760
We're on our way to find Yoka-chan now!

00:47.090 --> 00:48.210
That's right.

00:48.210 --> 00:50.290
I'd like to read Akira-chan's travelogue, too.

00:50.290 --> 00:53.280
I bet that old guy's just making stuff up.

00:53.280 --> 00:55.980
But he showed up in front of us 
when he was headed the other way.

00:56.420 --> 00:57.310
Could he have a twin?

00:57.310 --> 01:00.750
It's gonna happen. The end of the world.

01:01.030 --> 01:01.900
Then...

01:01.900 --> 01:04.240
Today might be my last chance for this.

01:04.240 --> 01:05.840
Cut it out with those hands!

01:05.840 --> 01:08.360
It's the last time, so I won't stop, 
even if you complain!

01:08.360 --> 01:14.970
Tickle, tickle!

01:10.890 --> 01:13.560
Stop before you start fighting!

01:30.270 --> 01:34.030
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

02:47.060 --> 02:49.390
Funny seeing you up here, Pochi-san.

02:49.720 --> 02:52.200
Two more stops until Ikebukuro.

02:49.730 --> 02:52.190
<b>Sakuradai</b>

02:49.730 --> 02:52.190
<b>Ekoda</b>

02:49.730 --> 02:52.190
<b>Higashi-Nagasaki</b>

02:49.730 --> 02:52.190
<b>Shiinamachi</b>

02:49.730 --> 02:52.190
<b>Ikebukuro</b>

02:52.200 --> 02:54.070
Have you caught Yoka's scent?

02:54.780 --> 02:56.740
Just here on a whim?

03:09.780 --> 03:11.280
Sorry, Nadeko-chan.

03:11.280 --> 03:12.030
Are you hurt?!

03:12.030 --> 03:13.630
I'm fine, I'm fine.

03:14.780 --> 03:15.610
What happened?!

03:15.610 --> 03:16.350
What?

03:15.720 --> 03:16.850
Shizuru-chan!

03:16.850 --> 03:18.300
There's something ahead.

03:22.250 --> 03:23.420
Animals?

03:23.420 --> 03:25.890
Of the stuffed variety?

03:25.890 --> 03:28.850
Episode 10       A True Symbol of Rebellion and Decadence

03:35.270 --> 03:36.830
They're not attacking?

03:36.830 --> 03:39.000
Any chance the chubby one's a kusamochi?

03:39.000 --> 03:41.680
I don't think so, but let's stay on guard.

03:50.640 --> 03:51.630
Huh?

03:52.790 --> 03:54.080
Dad?

03:55.790 --> 03:57.370
Don't worry!

03:57.370 --> 03:59.800
We're just going to check out 
some other towns.

03:59.800 --> 04:02.800
We'll be back as soon as we 
figure out why this happened.

04:02.800 --> 04:04.360
I reckon it'll take two hours.

04:04.830 --> 04:06.600
Two weeks at most.

04:08.450 --> 04:09.750
Wrong guy.

04:10.580 --> 04:11.570
Is that you, Shizuru?

04:11.570 --> 04:13.280
What? Not the wrong guy?!

04:13.280 --> 04:15.180
Oh! It's Shizuru, kyurun!

04:15.180 --> 04:17.400
Eisaku, Hide-bo, it's my daughter!

04:17.400 --> 04:19.010
That's Shizuru-chan, shupi?

04:19.010 --> 04:19.810
Oh, you're right!

04:19.810 --> 04:20.660
It's really her-ccho!

04:20.660 --> 04:22.330
Shizuru-chan's dad?!

04:22.330 --> 04:25.200
And the fire department folk 
who never came back.

04:25.200 --> 04:27.330
Reimi-chan and Akira-chan!

04:27.330 --> 04:28.400
Which means...

04:28.400 --> 04:30.040
This here's Nadeko-chan!

04:33.130 --> 04:34.570
That's Pochi-san.

04:34.570 --> 04:37.260
Oh, still not one for a joke, 
huh, Nadeko-chan?

04:37.750 --> 04:39.010
It's been much too long.

04:39.010 --> 04:40.320
Enough of that.

04:40.320 --> 04:43.240
Shizuru, you've grown big 
while I've been away, kyurun.

04:43.240 --> 04:45.200
You're the one who's shrunk, Dad.

04:45.200 --> 04:45.610
Nice one!

04:45.610 --> 04:46.770
No, it's not!

04:47.310 --> 04:48.560
Mister, mister!

04:48.560 --> 04:49.980
I've gotten pretty tall too, right?

04:49.980 --> 04:51.090
Sure have!

04:51.090 --> 04:52.650
Nadeko-chan's grown up as well.

04:52.650 --> 04:53.760
Akira-chan...

04:53.760 --> 04:55.720
Akira-chan's pretty much the same.

05:00.910 --> 05:03.020
Pochi-san's scarier than I remember.

05:03.020 --> 05:04.330
He's big enough to gobble me up, kyurun!

05:04.330 --> 05:05.300
Look, look!

05:05.300 --> 05:07.080
We drove that thing here! 
Isn't that awesome?

05:07.080 --> 05:10.030
That's one feisty ride you've got there.

05:10.030 --> 05:11.420
Not surprised at all, huh?

05:11.420 --> 05:12.960
Just look around you.

05:12.960 --> 05:14.840
It'll take more to make me 
quake in my boots.

05:14.840 --> 05:17.530
Oh, yeah. Mom said that if I ran into you,

05:17.530 --> 05:20.000
I'm to tell you to snap out 
of it and come home.

05:20.000 --> 05:21.500
<i>Now</i> he's quaking in his boots.

05:21.860 --> 05:22.760
Was she mad?

05:22.760 --> 05:23.720
She was fed up.

05:23.720 --> 05:24.730
What do I do?

05:24.730 --> 05:25.940
She's even scarier like that!

05:25.940 --> 05:26.480
Beats me.

05:26.480 --> 05:29.080
I told her I was going to just 
scope things out, kyurun.

05:29.080 --> 05:30.350
It's been two years.

05:30.350 --> 05:31.050
But, but...

05:31.050 --> 05:32.370
I've sent back a few letters!

05:32.370 --> 05:34.290
Those don't count as letters.

05:33.350 --> 05:35.180
<b></b>I'm gonna be a little longer

05:34.290 --> 05:35.180
Mom had no words.

05:36.380 --> 05:38.390
Is everyone in Agano doing well, shupi?

05:38.390 --> 05:39.570
Yeah, totally!

05:39.570 --> 05:42.420
Masaharu-san gets a little carnivorous 
once in a while, though.

05:42.420 --> 05:43.370
That's Masa for you.

05:43.370 --> 05:45.520
He's always been like that.

05:45.520 --> 05:47.770
Even we have our animal 
instincts take over at times.

05:47.770 --> 05:49.270
Masa-san's got it worse.

05:49.270 --> 05:51.820
So, what have you been doing all this time?

05:51.820 --> 05:52.850
Taking a break.

05:52.850 --> 05:55.060
Both we and our cart took 
a real beating, kyurun.

05:55.060 --> 05:57.320
Seriously, why do you keep saying "kyurun"?!

05:57.320 --> 05:58.930
And why do you look so round now?

05:58.930 --> 05:59.760
Oh, you noticed?

05:59.760 --> 06:00.870
Of course I did!

06:00.870 --> 06:01.450
Well?

06:01.450 --> 06:02.220
It's gross.

06:02.220 --> 06:05.080
That's why I was ignoring it, 
but it's even grosser that you won't stop.

06:05.080 --> 06:07.850
Watch your mouth! I'll get mad, 
even with your friends here!

06:07.850 --> 06:09.720
Chikura-san, she's right-ccho!

06:09.720 --> 06:12.970
It really is creepy to have old men 
going "kyurun" or "shupi"!

06:13.850 --> 06:16.730
We kinda... got turned into this.

06:17.050 --> 06:17.920
By who?

06:17.920 --> 06:19.420
The folks in Shiinamachi.

06:19.420 --> 06:20.070
Why?

06:20.070 --> 06:22.710
Well, we ran into a weird 
old guy on the way.

06:22.710 --> 06:24.620
Said Ikebukuro was a real mess.

06:24.620 --> 06:27.940
So we were on our way to check it out, and 
they picked a fight with us in Shiinamachi.

06:29.120 --> 06:31.330
I don't get it, but I turned all cute.

06:31.330 --> 06:32.210
So you lost?

06:32.210 --> 06:33.350
We didn't lose, kyurun!

06:33.350 --> 06:34.140
No more "kyurun"!

06:34.140 --> 06:37.370
If I wasn't an animal, I'd have trounced 
them with my Agano jiu-jutsu!

06:38.370 --> 06:39.880
I'm telling the truth!

06:39.880 --> 06:41.040
I got one of 'em good!

06:41.040 --> 06:42.120
Look! My battle trophy!

06:42.120 --> 06:43.690
A beret?

06:43.690 --> 06:45.210
They were all wearing these.

06:45.210 --> 06:45.760
Want it?

06:45.760 --> 06:46.470
No thanks.

06:46.470 --> 06:47.000
I do!

06:47.000 --> 06:47.690
Eh?

06:47.690 --> 06:49.200
Oh, take it. Here.

06:49.200 --> 06:51.220
Rampo, Guevara...

06:51.220 --> 06:53.250
A true symbol of rebellion and decadence!

06:53.250 --> 06:55.100
So, what about you?

06:55.100 --> 06:56.770
Did you come out here to find us?

06:56.770 --> 06:58.990
We're going to Ikebukuro.
To bring Yoka home.

06:58.990 --> 07:00.290
Yoka-chan?

07:00.290 --> 07:02.970
Chikura-san, so was that 
really Yoka-chan, shupi?

07:02.970 --> 07:03.990
You met her?!

07:03.990 --> 07:06.210
We saw her in Shiinamachi.

07:06.210 --> 07:07.480
But, well...

07:16.440 --> 07:19.420
She was like your mother coming home 
late after drinking.

07:19.420 --> 07:20.650
Like we'd know that.

07:20.650 --> 07:21.340
And?

07:21.340 --> 07:22.430
That's it.

07:22.430 --> 07:23.880
Things got hairy right after that.

07:24.170 --> 07:25.710
Think she's still in Shiinamachi?

07:25.710 --> 07:27.190
Who knows?

07:27.190 --> 07:29.010
Was it even really Yoka?!

07:29.010 --> 07:32.730
Well, when you put it like that, maybe not...

07:32.730 --> 07:33.430
Which is it?!

07:33.430 --> 07:35.010
I don't know, kyurun!

07:35.010 --> 07:36.690
I said, stop it with the "kyurun"!

07:36.690 --> 07:37.440
Um...

07:37.440 --> 07:39.690
Was there anything you noticed about her?

07:40.980 --> 07:43.520
Oh, she really grew out her hair.

07:43.520 --> 07:44.840
It was long to begin with!

07:44.840 --> 07:46.680
Hey, it almost reached the ground!

07:46.960 --> 07:49.450
That can't have been Yoka, then.

07:49.450 --> 07:51.810
Yoka cuts her own hair.

07:51.810 --> 07:53.480
She's real good at it, too.

07:55.630 --> 07:57.250
Thanks a lot, really.

07:57.250 --> 07:59.730
You have short arms, 
so it's the least we could do.

07:59.730 --> 08:01.150
Oh, it's Zenjiro-san!

08:01.150 --> 08:02.460
I forgot!

08:02.460 --> 08:03.900
I couldn't hear it at all.

08:03.900 --> 08:05.250
That's Reimi-chan for you.

08:05.250 --> 08:06.140
Zenjiro?

08:06.140 --> 08:07.680
Did he get better, kyurun?

08:09.500 --> 08:12.270
Currently past Higashi-Nagasaki.

08:12.930 --> 08:15.220
Sounds like they found Shizuru's father.

08:15.220 --> 08:16.980
That's not important now!

08:16.980 --> 08:18.370
You need to tell them what matters!

08:18.370 --> 08:19.690
I know that!

08:20.060 --> 08:21.360
Um...

08:21.360 --> 08:25.440
"Stay the course and the 
world will... disappear"?!

08:25.440 --> 08:27.240
So it really <i>was</i> true.

08:27.240 --> 08:33.590
"However, put an end to it 
and turn world normal again"?

08:34.340 --> 08:36.660
Maybe we can turn the world back to normal!

08:38.150 --> 08:44.090
"Possible if you stop 7G 
gone haywire in Ikebukuro."

08:44.090 --> 08:45.540
Seriously? It's that easy?

08:45.970 --> 08:47.210
Just wait.

08:47.950 --> 08:50.180
"Looking into a way now..."

08:50.180 --> 08:53.620
"Once we find out, will let you kno—
choo choo-choo..."

08:54.300 --> 08:56.180
The hell's he mean by "choo choo-choo"?

08:56.180 --> 08:58.030
He still can't talk for long.

08:58.030 --> 08:59.670
Although it's not as bad now.

08:59.670 --> 09:02.080
What's this about turning 
the world normal again?

09:02.080 --> 09:05.120
You mean, if we do something in Ikebukuro, 
I can go back to being human?!

09:05.120 --> 09:09.160
I'm not sure, but he did say Ikebukuro 
was their stronghold or whatever before.

09:09.160 --> 09:11.390
Then I'll go with you, kyurun!

09:11.710 --> 09:14.150
Those beret guys might get 
in our way like before.

09:14.150 --> 09:15.610
You don't need to come with us.

09:15.610 --> 09:17.480
I'd be worried if you kids went alone!

09:17.480 --> 09:18.530
We'll be fine.

09:18.530 --> 09:19.880
I'm still human, you know.

09:19.880 --> 09:20.960
I'm going!

09:20.960 --> 09:21.770
You really don't have to!

09:21.770 --> 09:24.970
I can't leave something this important 
to my daughter and her friends!

09:24.970 --> 09:27.160
We're just going to meet Yoka!

09:27.160 --> 09:29.510
We might be able to turn 
the world back to normal!

09:29.510 --> 09:31.340
That doesn't matter!

09:31.340 --> 09:32.670
What?

09:32.670 --> 09:35.160
I mean, it does! But I don't care!

09:35.160 --> 09:36.260
Kyurun?

09:38.560 --> 09:40.350
It's fine, mister.

09:40.350 --> 09:42.050
Shizuru-chan's really strong.

09:42.050 --> 09:44.880
Maybe she is, but still...

09:44.880 --> 09:46.750
I can use a bow,

09:46.750 --> 09:48.620
Akira-chan's a snappy thinker,

09:48.620 --> 09:50.210
and Reimi-chan can just plain snap.

09:50.210 --> 09:50.980
I'll snap real good.

09:50.980 --> 09:52.680
Show 'em some sexy violence.

09:52.680 --> 09:56.080
You look weaker than when 
you were a real wolverine.

09:56.080 --> 09:58.300
And what's more, you're hurt.

09:58.870 --> 10:01.310
If it looks like we can change 
the world back, we will.

10:01.310 --> 10:03.270
That's one laid-back attitude...

10:03.270 --> 10:04.530
Chikura-san.

10:04.940 --> 10:09.970
Girls grow up a lot faster in 
two years than you'd think, shupi.

10:09.970 --> 10:12.900
Have faith in your daughter and let them go.

10:12.900 --> 10:16.410
We should go back to Agano and 
put our families at ease first.

10:16.700 --> 10:19.070
Go and see Mom again.

10:19.070 --> 10:22.800
It'll be too late once you fully turn 
into animals and can't talk.

10:24.180 --> 10:28.930
I guess you've got this in the bag 
with the Agano jiu-jitsu I taught you.

10:29.240 --> 10:29.990
Okay!

10:29.990 --> 10:30.980
Go on, Shizuru!

10:30.980 --> 10:32.920
Avenge your father!

10:35.460 --> 10:37.290
Bye-bye!

10:36.410 --> 10:38.160
Please be careful!

10:38.160 --> 10:39.040
Thanks!

10:38.160 --> 10:39.040
Yeah!

10:39.040 --> 10:39.940
You too!

10:44.270 --> 10:47.330
Get 'em good!

10:47.630 --> 10:50.430
What you said earlier really got to me.

10:50.430 --> 10:52.960
That's what it means to have a family.

10:52.960 --> 10:54.180
You said it.

10:54.180 --> 10:55.610
Even though you're a bachelor.

10:55.610 --> 10:57.940
Okay, let's get this cart 
back on the tracks!

10:57.940 --> 10:59.300
Yessir!

11:02.850 --> 11:06.230
Man, Shizuru-chan's dad 
hasn't changed at all.

11:06.230 --> 11:07.960
As big of an idiot as always.

11:07.960 --> 11:09.590
I thought he was really funny.

11:10.010 --> 11:13.090
Wait, what about the tracks 
past Higashi-Agano?

11:13.090 --> 11:14.320
The part that's uncrossable now.

11:14.320 --> 11:15.810
I'm sure the water's gone down.

11:15.810 --> 11:17.640
If not, they'll come up with something.

11:17.640 --> 11:18.580
You think so?

11:18.580 --> 11:21.200
Dad'll be fine. Even if he <i>is</i> an idiot.

11:21.800 --> 11:23.100
That's true.

11:23.100 --> 11:24.940
Oh, not the idiot part.

11:26.120 --> 11:29.670
You know, what does turning 
the world normal again mean?

11:29.670 --> 11:31.290
I don't really get it.

11:31.290 --> 11:33.300
Isn't it exactly what it sounds like?

11:33.300 --> 11:36.510
I think he means going back 
to how things were before 7G.

11:37.160 --> 11:40.510
Honestly, I don't know which I prefer now.

11:40.510 --> 11:43.240
I <i>did</i> want things to go 
back if it was possible,

11:43.240 --> 11:45.170
but I'd already kinda given up.

11:45.170 --> 11:47.260
Things now are pretty 
chill in their own way.

11:48.160 --> 11:50.400
My travelogue is ending up 
more and more chaotic.

11:51.600 --> 11:52.820
Shizuru-chan.

11:53.530 --> 11:56.510
I think worse than the world 
not going back to normal

11:56.510 --> 11:59.410
would be you and Yoka-chan 
not going back to how you were.

11:59.410 --> 12:00.400
Me too!

12:00.400 --> 12:00.860
Yeah.

12:04.530 --> 12:08.710
Besides, there's no way we can 
stop 7G from running wild.

12:08.710 --> 12:10.380
We don't know that yet.

12:10.380 --> 12:14.370
We could suddenly wake up one day 
and find out we have incredible powers.

12:14.370 --> 12:15.520
Like what?

12:19.720 --> 12:21.970
O sacred bitter melon!

12:21.970 --> 12:25.210
Gather within me and unleash 
your bitter meloning power!

12:32.930 --> 12:34.720
Nothing happened.

12:34.720 --> 12:35.650
Akira, you fraud.

12:36.570 --> 12:38.360
Ah, that's mine!

12:39.570 --> 12:40.390
Give it back!

12:40.390 --> 12:40.890
Yum.

12:40.890 --> 12:41.760
Spit it out!

12:41.760 --> 12:42.570
Okay, I will.

12:42.570 --> 12:43.730
Don't spit it out!

12:43.010 --> 12:44.820
Play nice!

12:52.260 --> 12:55.360
Hey, the weather's gotten worse.

12:55.800 --> 12:58.300
The sky's suddenly gone dark with clouds.

12:58.300 --> 12:59.930
It was clear just a minute ago.

12:59.930 --> 13:01.900
Oh, you're right.

13:01.900 --> 13:03.040
Over there.

13:03.040 --> 13:03.430
Huh?

13:03.430 --> 13:05.010
Is that Shiinamachi Station?

13:05.010 --> 13:05.800
Yeah.

13:05.800 --> 13:06.330
What do we do?

13:06.680 --> 13:07.900
What do you mean?

13:07.900 --> 13:09.300
Should we keep going?

13:09.300 --> 13:11.870
Shizuru's dad said they attacked him.

13:13.160 --> 13:14.040
Let's go past it!

13:14.040 --> 13:14.700
Okay!

13:14.700 --> 13:16.190
I'll go tell Shizuru-chan and the others.

13:16.190 --> 13:17.620
Oh, you were awake—

13:22.860 --> 13:24.120
Reimi-chan!

13:24.120 --> 13:25.730
What the heck?

13:28.380 --> 13:31.270
We can't get to Ikebukuro like this...

13:38.740 --> 13:40.360
Ugh, I don't want to get off.

13:40.360 --> 13:42.170
I just know we're gonna 
run into some weirdos.

13:42.170 --> 13:43.420
Either way, we can't move on.

13:43.420 --> 13:44.330
It's fine!

13:44.330 --> 13:46.160
I'm stronger than my dad.

13:46.160 --> 13:46.840
Really?

13:46.840 --> 13:47.860
Not that I'd know!

13:47.860 --> 13:49.630
Why'd I get my hopes up?

13:49.140 --> 13:51.600
<b></b>Shiinamachi

13:49.140 --> 13:51.600
<b>Sun Road</b>

13:55.250 --> 13:57.010
There's nobody here.

13:57.340 --> 13:58.950
Not even the police.

13:58.940 --> 14:01.400
<b>Dissidents Yesterday




Egg Custards




Arrestees</b>

13:58.940 --> 14:01.400
<b>People




People</b>

14:00.010 --> 14:01.390
Egg custard?

14:01.390 --> 14:03.010
You're right, egg custard.

14:03.010 --> 14:04.250
What does that mean?

14:05.030 --> 14:06.760
Steamed to death like egg custard.

14:06.760 --> 14:08.840
Torture akin to Goemon 
boiling alive in a cauldron.

14:08.840 --> 14:09.310
Oh, no!

14:09.070 --> 14:11.080
<b>Dissidents Yesterday





Egg Custards





Arrestees</b>

14:09.310 --> 14:10.850
That's scary! Cut it ou—

14:11.300 --> 14:13.250
Something's stuck to my face!

14:14.030 --> 14:15.560
The Fukuro Times?

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>Poison</b>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>Pontaro</b>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>Stays</b>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>On</b>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>As</b>

14:16.040 --> 14:17.290
<b>Mayor</b>

14:16.380 --> 14:17.300
Wait...

14:17.650 --> 14:18.790
Isn't this Yoka-chan?!

14:19.320 --> 14:20.510
"Early on the third,"

14:20.510 --> 14:24.730
"Her Majesty Queen Yoka of Nakatomi attended 
an astronomy learning session..."

14:24.730 --> 14:25.910
They're calling her a queen!

14:26.600 --> 14:29.000
If this really is Yoka-chan...

14:29.000 --> 14:31.370
She looks a little too scary 
to be Yoka-chan.

14:31.370 --> 14:32.100
A rebellious phase?

14:32.360 --> 14:33.890
Who are these people next to her?

14:33.890 --> 14:35.650
They look like bad guys!

14:35.650 --> 14:40.200
Are these the people in power who don't 
want the world to go back to normal?

14:41.630 --> 14:43.100
So it's you!

14:43.100 --> 14:45.500
The ones trying to reach Ikebukuro!

14:45.820 --> 14:48.950
Unfortunately, we can't 
let you go to Ikebukuro.

14:48.950 --> 14:52.270
Your path ends here in Shiinamachi, 
where you'll become our art!

14:52.270 --> 14:53.390
Huh? What's that mean?

14:53.390 --> 14:55.050
Become their art...

14:55.050 --> 14:57.690
In other words, we're going 
to serve as their art models.

14:57.690 --> 15:00.720
They'll probably strip us naked 
and do pervy stuff to us!

15:00.720 --> 15:01.820
You're awful!

15:01.820 --> 15:02.740
No, we won't!

15:02.030 --> 15:03.740
Oh, that hat!

15:03.740 --> 15:05.720
They're probably the ones who attacked Dad!

15:05.720 --> 15:08.090
Wait, that's the kusamochi 
from the hermit's map!

15:08.090 --> 15:09.160
Ah! You there!

15:09.160 --> 15:10.460
That beret!

15:10.460 --> 15:13.040
That's the one those weird 
animals stole from Mr. T!

15:13.040 --> 15:13.640
Give it back!

15:13.640 --> 15:14.190
No way!

15:14.190 --> 15:15.300
Grr!

15:15.300 --> 15:20.140
It looks like you kids ruined the story 
we set up for Oizumi-gakuen!

15:20.140 --> 15:21.450
Oizumi-gakuen?

15:21.450 --> 15:22.680
Story?

15:22.680 --> 15:23.540
<i>NeriAli</i>?

15:23.540 --> 15:24.440
Hey, wait!

15:24.440 --> 15:27.350
So the ones who made a big mess 
of the world of <i>NeriAli</i>...

15:27.350 --> 15:28.500
Exactly!

15:28.500 --> 15:30.480
Alice posed too large of a threat.

15:30.480 --> 15:34.380
Her charisma could have meant 
danger for Ikebukuro!

15:34.380 --> 15:36.300
So it's <i>your</i> fault that Alice died?!

15:36.300 --> 15:36.860
You'll pay!

15:36.860 --> 15:38.400
That's <i>my</i> line!

15:39.990 --> 15:41.960
Gekiga Beam!

15:43.350 --> 15:44.620
Nadeko-chan!

15:46.460 --> 15:47.570
Oh, my.

15:47.570 --> 15:49.010
I'm perfectly fine.

15:49.010 --> 15:50.400
No, you're not!

15:50.400 --> 15:51.940
She's way over the top now.

15:52.300 --> 15:53.560
Over the top in what fashion?!

15:53.560 --> 15:55.630
Good heavens! What has befallen me?!

15:55.630 --> 15:59.060
Her mind will soon turn into that 
of the character we invented, as well!

15:59.060 --> 16:00.000
Turn her back right now!

16:00.000 --> 16:01.210
No can do!

16:01.210 --> 16:03.430
You can stop its progress 
by leaving this town.

16:03.430 --> 16:04.730
Just turn back already!

16:05.380 --> 16:07.930
It'll be faster to kick their butts 
with Agano jiu-jitsu.

16:07.930 --> 16:08.960
If you <i>can</i>, that is!

16:08.960 --> 16:11.740
Your serialization gets axed here!

16:13.240 --> 16:14.840
You're cruisin' for a bruisin' now!

16:14.840 --> 16:16.360
I'll send ya to hell!

16:16.360 --> 16:18.300
Hold it! There!

16:20.370 --> 16:21.210
Wuh-oh!

16:21.210 --> 16:23.240
I can't use my jiu-jitsu!

16:22.210 --> 16:23.240
But you're one cute cat.

16:23.240 --> 16:24.160
I dig it.

16:24.160 --> 16:26.480
We must protect Akira-chan at all costs!

16:26.480 --> 16:28.000
What character will I get turned into?

16:28.000 --> 16:29.150
If I could pick, ukiyo-e?

16:29.150 --> 16:32.310
Or maybe something avant-garde, 
like futurism?

16:32.310 --> 16:34.310
My new serialization begins here!

16:36.610 --> 16:37.940
Hmph!

16:37.940 --> 16:38.480
What?!

16:38.480 --> 16:40.070
Fauvism!

16:40.420 --> 16:41.440
Cubism!

16:41.440 --> 16:44.100
German expressionism!

16:45.160 --> 16:46.150
What?!

16:48.620 --> 16:49.490
Something came out!

16:49.490 --> 16:51.050
Mr. F!

16:53.480 --> 16:54.350
I'm scared! I'm scared!

16:54.350 --> 16:55.230
What is this?

16:55.230 --> 16:57.630
What <i>is</i> this?!

16:57.630 --> 17:01.180
So you know how to use 
the powers of the beret?!

17:03.320 --> 17:04.470
That's right.

17:04.470 --> 17:05.770
Surreal Bomber!

17:05.770 --> 17:07.190
Oh, she's just pretendin' she knew.

17:07.190 --> 17:08.310
I can tell.

17:08.310 --> 17:10.160
So the beret possesses powers, they say.

17:10.160 --> 17:12.100
Maybe that's our key to victowy!

17:12.100 --> 17:16.190
Hah! Your pitiful imaginations don't 
stand a chance against us mangaka!

17:16.190 --> 17:17.250
Take this!

17:17.250 --> 17:18.460
Yeah!

17:18.460 --> 17:19.840
Uh-huh!

17:24.780 --> 17:26.480
Hi-yah!

17:35.210 --> 17:36.240
See that?

17:36.240 --> 17:39.700
That's the imagination of Akira, 
the gloomy bookwor—

17:40.320 --> 17:41.400
What <i>is</i> this?

17:41.400 --> 17:42.150
It makes no sense!

17:42.150 --> 17:44.510
You're breaking the conventions here!

17:44.510 --> 17:45.780
What's the big idea, Akira?

17:45.780 --> 17:46.470
Try it out.

17:46.470 --> 17:47.780
Your thoughts will come to life.

17:47.780 --> 17:48.760
Okay.

17:48.760 --> 17:51.150
BL Flash!

17:54.340 --> 17:56.330
Mr. F, are you okay?

17:56.600 --> 17:59.010
Don't look at me like that, Mr. A...

17:59.010 --> 18:00.030
Mr. F...

17:59.010 --> 18:01.020
What in the world?

18:00.030 --> 18:01.030
Mr. A...

18:01.020 --> 18:01.620
I like it!

18:01.620 --> 18:02.840
Very nice!

18:03.080 --> 18:04.890
Sparkly Spur!

18:07.470 --> 18:08.320
What's this?

18:08.320 --> 18:10.050
I suddenly feel like I shouldn't be here...

18:10.050 --> 18:11.940
Like there's no demand for us!

18:11.940 --> 18:13.770
Hey, that's not true!

18:13.770 --> 18:15.130
Hot-Bwooded Fire!

18:15.130 --> 18:16.380
Pew pew!

18:19.080 --> 18:20.880
We're going to lose at this rate!

18:20.880 --> 18:21.950
Time to show our guts and fight!

18:21.950 --> 18:23.070
Prepare yourselves!

18:23.070 --> 18:24.490
I'll follow you to the ends of the Earth!

18:24.490 --> 18:26.300
We don't need no stinking berets!

18:31.000 --> 18:31.630
It can't be!

18:31.630 --> 18:33.100
What sloppy plotting!

18:33.100 --> 18:34.640
It's sacrilege! Utter sacrilege!

18:34.640 --> 18:37.300
Why are you twying to stop us, anyway?

18:37.300 --> 18:38.340
Yeah, exactamundo!

18:38.340 --> 18:41.920
Is it 'cause we got that charisma thing 
you were jawin' about with Alice?

18:41.920 --> 18:43.000
Not in the slightest!

18:43.000 --> 18:45.800
We were given the powers of the beret, 
so we have to follow orders!

18:45.800 --> 18:46.430
That's all it is!

18:46.430 --> 18:48.230
You were given powers? Truly?

18:48.230 --> 18:49.730
What's aww that about?

18:49.730 --> 18:51.650
It seems we have no choice...

18:51.650 --> 18:53.650
but to tell our tale.

18:53.650 --> 18:54.980
You can keep it to yerselves!

18:54.980 --> 18:56.450
Just answer our questions.

18:56.450 --> 18:57.970
How many years ago was it?

18:57.970 --> 18:59.190
I just said, save it!

18:59.690 --> 19:02.940
We came to this place with grand ambitions!

19:02.940 --> 19:04.710
We'll change the world with manga!

19:05.950 --> 19:08.890
But for some reason, our art 
styles weren't well-received,

19:08.890 --> 19:10.960
and they weren't popular in the least.

19:10.960 --> 19:14.000
Days and months of fruitless effort passed by.

19:14.000 --> 19:16.640
Stories should follow convention.

19:16.640 --> 19:18.830
Clichés are what move people the most.

19:18.830 --> 19:21.970
But those no-good editors dismissed us, 
calling us out-of-date...

19:21.970 --> 19:23.150
Wait, what?!

19:23.150 --> 19:23.850
Seriously?

19:23.850 --> 19:25.560
You're seriously going to 
skip the explanation?!

19:25.560 --> 19:27.090
No one moves during a flashback!

19:27.090 --> 19:28.710
That's convention, right there!

19:28.710 --> 19:31.510
We haven't even gotten to 7G happening!

19:31.510 --> 19:33.400
Or how these powers are a paid subscription,

19:33.400 --> 19:36.690
or the most important part, 
who gave us them!

19:36.690 --> 19:38.940
We'll manage somehow.

19:38.940 --> 19:39.970
D'oh!

19:39.970 --> 19:41.940
Artistic expression has no limits!

19:47.830 --> 19:51.240
Even if changing times lead to 
all sorts of constraints...

19:51.240 --> 19:53.250
New forms of expression 
in manga will be born!

19:53.250 --> 19:56.230
We were the ones who had given up all along!

19:56.230 --> 19:58.020
They've found enlightenment somehow.

19:58.020 --> 20:00.830
A matter of no import. 
Return us to normal posthaste.

20:00.830 --> 20:01.690
Hey, hey!

20:01.690 --> 20:02.920
Have you seen this girl befowe?

20:05.610 --> 20:07.660
You really <i>do</i> know the queen?!

20:07.660 --> 20:08.960
Yoka's our fwiend!

20:08.960 --> 20:10.590
We're on our way to find her!

20:10.590 --> 20:11.310
That's absurd!

20:11.310 --> 20:15.070
She's not someone who 
nobodies like you can meet!

20:15.070 --> 20:18.480
They say the queen is the mother 
of Ikebukuro as we know it,

20:18.480 --> 20:22.210
not to mention the mighty being 
who gave us these powers!

20:23.780 --> 20:27.670
You're a threat to the queen 
and this very world itself!

20:27.670 --> 20:29.320
That's what Pontaro-sama told us!

20:29.320 --> 20:30.130
Pontaro?

20:30.130 --> 20:30.870
Who's that?

20:30.870 --> 20:32.570
You can see him right there!

20:32.570 --> 20:34.620
The not-so-tall one next to her!

20:35.000 --> 20:36.350
Pontaro...

20:36.350 --> 20:37.990
Anyway, if you value your lives,

20:37.990 --> 20:40.500
don't do anything to upset the queen!

20:40.500 --> 20:42.340
She'll turn you into egg custard!

20:42.340 --> 20:47.350
<b>Dissidents Yesterday




Egg Custards




Arrestees</b>

20:42.340 --> 20:47.350
<b>People




People</b>

20:42.630 --> 20:45.280
We saw the same term on the police box. 
Whatever does it mean?

20:45.280 --> 20:46.330
Literally what it says!

20:46.330 --> 20:47.740
It really was a form of torture...

20:47.740 --> 20:49.960
Yoka-chan would never do that!

20:49.960 --> 20:52.530
Pontaro! I wemember now!

20:52.530 --> 20:54.750
Zenjiro-san mentioned him!

20:54.750 --> 20:57.100
That damn rotten dunghead Pontaro!

20:57.100 --> 20:59.220
How many times did I tell him 
to give up on 7G?

20:59.490 --> 21:02.190
So he's the one wesponsible for 7G?

21:02.190 --> 21:03.400
For real?

21:03.400 --> 21:06.220
What's Yoka-chan doin' with a fink like him?

21:06.220 --> 21:07.880
I weally don't know!

21:07.880 --> 21:09.020
An evil vizier!

21:09.020 --> 21:10.400
A weevil is here?

21:10.400 --> 21:11.090
What d'ya mean?

21:11.090 --> 21:14.400
You mean Yoka-chan is being 
hoodwinked by that scoundrel?

21:14.400 --> 21:16.100
Or rather, being manipulated by him?

21:16.100 --> 21:18.870
But the Yoka-chan we know 
would never trust him.

21:19.610 --> 21:20.800
7G...

21:21.150 --> 21:23.610
There is a chance that it plays a role here.

21:23.610 --> 21:27.250
Then that means we definitely need 
to put a stop to it, does it not?

21:27.250 --> 21:29.000
This is way over my head, dudettes.

21:35.370 --> 21:36.620
We're back to normal!

21:36.620 --> 21:37.790
Seems like it.

21:37.790 --> 21:40.550
We canceled the subscription for our powers.

21:40.550 --> 21:43.250
Fine by me. That thing cost a fortune.

21:59.890 --> 22:01.040
So that's...

22:01.850 --> 22:03.210
Ikebukuro...
